text:
Hi everyone! I’m looking for someone who has experience inviting first-degree relatives of a partner who has Alef/5 status to Israel.

We want to invite my husband’s parents. My husband is currently on Alef/5, and as far as I understand from document 5.4.0001, in order for them to visit, we need to apply in advance to the Ministry of the Interior and obtain an entry permit.

I’m trying to figure out exactly which set of documents needs to be attached to the application.

So far, this is how I understand it:
— proof of family relationship (presumably my husband’s birth certificate?)
— round-trip tickets;
— travel insurance for the duration of the trip;
— a letter from the parents’ employer;
— a bank statement from their account confirming they have sufficient funds for the trip;
— or our own financial documents/bank statement, if we indicate that we’re covering the expenses ourselves.

What else were you asked to provide?

I’d be very grateful if anyone could share their real-life experience and, especially, the list of documents they submitted.
